v3.0.1.0

Builds on current systems: OpenSSL 3, Boost 1.66 to 1.92, GCC 13+, Clang/Xcode, Qt 5.15, miniupnpc 2.2.8+
Added - GitHub Actions builds for Linux, Windows and macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel)
Faster sync - 500 blocks per getblocks request (was 50)
Faster sync - sync peer is chosen and replaced when it stalls or disconnects (was the first peer to connect, forever)
Faster sync - stall watchdog asks again after 60s without a new block, switches peer after two stalls
Faster sync - blocks offered by the sync peer are requested immediately (no 2 minute retry delay)
Faster sync - larger database cache by default (-dbcache=100)
Memory - orphan blocks capped (-maxorphanblocksmib, default 40)
Memory - getdata requests answered as the send buffer drains instead of all at once
Memory - old block/transaction requests are forgotten; per-peer request queue capped
Memory - orphan transaction pool limited to 1000
Fix - key copies kept the wrong compressed flag; bad keys leaked memory
Fix - MultiSend tried to send a transaction that failed to be created
Fix - -testnet failed at startup (genesis block)
Added - -blockbatchsize option


